# ---------------------------------------------------------- personal data
# The gallery holds face embeddings of named, identifiable people, and the
# baseline holds their names alongside reference match scores. Biometric
# identifiers are not ours to publish. Excluding them costs a clone nothing it
# should not pay: enroll.py builds a gallery from your own photos, and every
# consumer already fails with instructions when these are absent.
db/embeddings.npz
db/baseline.json
db/*.backup.*
dataset/

# db/config.json IS tracked on purpose -- threshold plus aggregate metrics,
# no names. It is what makes the README's numbers checkable.

# ------------------------------------------------------- internal documents
# Handover notes: robot addresses, login details, colleague names, site
# specifics. Useful locally, not publishable, and scrubbing it would remove
# the reason it exists. README.md is the public document.
context.md

# ------------------------------------------------------------------- models
# ~53 MB of ONNX, and fully reproducible: install.sh fetches buffalo_s from
# the InsightFace release and prunes the parts we do not use.
models/

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ secrets
# Robot host/user/password live outside the repo. See .fr_robots.env.example
.fr_robots.env

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- generated
venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
log.log
output/
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.png

# Test traces from the locomotion work (~/fr_tests also holds these)
*.csv

# Local safety copies
.fr_backup_*/
.fr_prepush_*/
face_recognition_ws.bak.*/

# Saved-aside git histories. These MUST stay out: a .git directory's objects
# contain blobs of everything it ever tracked -- including the gallery and the
# passworded handover notes this .gitignore exists to exclude. Committing one
# would smuggle the whole lot back in as loose objects. Caught exactly that on
# 2026-09-03: 66 of 93 tracked files were a saved .git.bak.
.git.bak*/
*.git.bak/

# Symlink into an ignored backup directory -- meaningless in a clone.
.fr_backup_latest
